# S8-1 (PROBE): the first attach of EIGHT SEATS on two 64-row M3 blocks, on the AUDITED gate profile c2-packed-tp4-8-gate (c2-packed-tp4-8 plus the
# verify T1 and T2 audits, the gate marker and the gate limits; QWEN_FAST_M3_BLOCKS=2, max-num-seqs 8, 16,416 KV blocks, a 512 MiB trace region).
# An all-four reset, then the smoke: warmup, one coding stream, concurrent4_solo, concurrent4_code_equal (the same four prompts as S8-0: flag ON
# against flag OFF), concurrent8_code (4k, 8k, 16k, 24k twice: queues nobody, both blocks packed), concurrent8_code_equal (eight 4k code prompts,
# 800 out: the audited exactness shape for both blocks), concurrent5_split (user 4 alone in block B for 320 tokens, then a sixth into B: the split
# round and the narrowing) and concurrent8_drain (budgets 200 to 1,600 with ignore_eos: live goes 8 to 1 through every split the placement allows).
# EARLY KILL SIGNALS, in this order (the window stops at the first and the handback runs):
# (1) the attach: '[PINDIAG] packed-any admission passed:' with no UNQUALIFIED line; 'extent block engaged: blocks=2 segments=4,4'; block B compiled
# ZERO programs after block A's trace capture (the program count logged before and after block B: a block built after a capture lands in the holes the
# capture freed and every replay overwrites it); DRAM after attach about 22.7 to 23.0 GB per chip.
# (2) concurrent8_code_equal: ZERO audit mismatches (T1, T2, extent) and the block-B users (users 4 to 7) equal to their solo answers (S8-2a is the strict
# gate for that; here the audits are the claim).
# (3) concurrent4_code_equal: every hash EQUAL to S8-0's (the flag changes nothing at four or fewer live: the same-program claim). A difference stops
# I1.
# (4) rounds with live = 8 were seen, and the mixed-round markers (one live user in a block while the other runs packed) are present in
# concurrent5_split and concurrent8_drain.
# NOT CARRIED: the design asks S8-1 for QWEN_FAST_TRACE_CENSUS=1 (graph off) to see the allocator around each capture. A job file carries a profile and
# no environment, and the eight-seat profiles are pinned to their named deltas, so the census view is NOT taken here; the construction-order evidence
# above (the program counts around block B) is read from the attach log instead. The census view is taken on the diag twin (S8-3a), which carries it.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; the first eight-engine attach and build 15-35 min (cold kernel cache); the eight tests 30-50 min: 60 / 80 / 100 min.
# Stop rule: any attach refusal, a hang, garbage text, an errored or empty stream, an audit mismatch or a difference from S8-0 stops the window.
# SHIP WINDOW: on the shipping image, so the S8-0 against S8-1 hash equality is read inside one image. The request warm
# (QWEN_FAST_M3_REQUEST_WARM=1, in this profile) is the confirmed fix for the first-request-engine hang: the log must show the warm line before
# 'packed blocks capture block=0'. The first run of this job (before the fix) hung; a pass on the fix image is v261's, repeated here on the shipped bytes.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8 SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8 is the SHIPPING image: the base SB8 builds
# from this branch with the eight-seat profile baked in as its serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its
# seat count (ENV THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP). Every job serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still
# names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default. A commit that changes a file the image carries needs a new SB8 build and a
# new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_solo,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent8_code,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
